# The oldest installed Supavise version that may upgrade straight to the release being built.
# deploy/release-assets.sh writes it into the signed release manifest as min_upgrade_from, and
# `supavise upgrade` and `supavise self-update` refuse to skip past it: a node on an older
# version installs this version first. Raise it in the commit that makes a release depend on
# something the previous ones did not do (a data migration that is not backward compatible, a
# removed unit, a changed on-disk layout); leave it alone otherwise. v0.1.0, v0.1.1 and v0.1.3 are
# released and each may upgrade straight to the release being built (a v0.1.x registry is migrated
# by the first start of the new daemon), so no version is excluded.
v0.0.0
